Avenue A from the SOTA-avenues analysis: does flipping CARNOT_ARC_TRUST_METRIC=cell_recall lift live
first-win? Cross-tabulated the two existing per-game probes. The flag governs the e3 LLM/DSL-induction
path, where 0/6 gap-1 games are exact-FAIL+cell_recall-PASS -- the induced models have cell_recall ~0
(cn04 0.015, cd82 0.0), so the gate decision is identical under both metrics -> agent byte-identical ->
first-win provably unchanged. Induction QUALITY is the wall, not the gate. (No LLM run needed; gate-pass
data proves it.) Sharper untested lever surfaced: the TTT learned-dynamics path flips 4 games FAIL->PASS
(ka59 0.91/sc25 0.80/tn36 0.87/lp85 0.59) -- route live trust to TTT dynamics there, GPU-gated follow-on.
